{"type":"standard","title":"Janelle Stelson","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Janelle Stelson</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q136368691","titles":{"canonical":"Janelle_Stelson","normalized":"Janelle Stelson","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Janelle Stelson</span></span>"},"pageid":76721287,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Janelle_Stelson_08-29-2026_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Janelle_Stelson_08-29-2026_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":434},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Janelle_Stelson_08-29-2026_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":736,"height":967},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1378816202","tid":"31af85e1-c15a-11f1-a666-674fccd69ad7","timestamp":"2026-10-06T07:47:35Z","description":"American television news anchor","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janelle_Stelson","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janelle_Stelson?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janelle_Stelson?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Janelle_Stelson"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janelle_Stelson","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Janelle_Stelson","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janelle_Stelson?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Janelle_Stelson"}},"extract":"Janelle Stelson is an American former television news anchor and politician. She worked as a television journalist in Pennsylvania for more than three decades, including 26 years as an anchor at WGAL-TV in Lancaster. Stelson was the Democratic nominee for Pennsylvania's 10th congressional district in 2024, narrowly losing to incumbent Republican Scott Perry, and is the party's nominee again in the 2026 election.","extract_html":"<p><b>Janelle Stelson</b> is an American former television news anchor and politician. She worked as a television journalist in Pennsylvania for more than three decades, including 26 years as an anchor at WGAL-TV in Lancaster. Stelson was the Democratic nominee for Pennsylvania's 10th congressional district in 2024, narrowly losing to incumbent Republican Scott Perry, and is the party's nominee again in the 2026 election.</p>"}